".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-OCA%2Fpurchase--workflow-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/OCA/purchase-workflow/tree/20.0/purchase_request_alternative\n"
"    :alt: OCA/purchase-workflow\n"
".. |badge4| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/weblate-Translate%20me-F47D42.png\n"
"    :target: https://translation.odoo-community.org/projects/purchase-workflow-20-0/purchase-workflow-20-0-purchase_request_alternative\n"
"    :alt: Translate me on Weblate\n"
".. |badge5| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/runboat-Try%20me-875A7B.png\n"
"    :target: https://runboat.odoo-community.org/builds?repo=OCA/purchase-workflow&target_branch=20.0\n"
"    :alt: Try me on Runboat\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3| |badge4| |badge5|\n"
"\n"
"When a request for quotation (RFQ) is created from a purchase request\n"
"with ``purchase_request``, each RFQ line keeps a link to the purchase\n"
"request lines it covers. That link is what lets the purchase request\n"
"follow the purchase: it shows the RFQ, moves to *Purchased* when the\n"
"order is confirmed and tracks the received quantities through\n"
"allocations.\n"
"\n"
"The standard *Create Alternative* action of ``purchase_alternative``\n"
"builds new RFQs for other vendors by copying the product lines of the\n"
"original RFQ, but the copies lose the link to the purchase request. If\n"
"an alternative RFQ ends up being the one confirmed, the purchase request\n"
"never learns about it.\n"
"\n"
"This module propagates the purchase request lines and their allocations\n"
"to the lines of every alternative RFQ created with *Create Alternative*,\n"
"so the purchase request follows whichever RFQ wins the comparison.\n"
"\n"
"It is installed automatically when both ``purchase_request`` and\n"
"``purchase_alternative`` are installed.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"1. Approve a purchase request and create an RFQ from its lines (*Create\n"
"   RFQ* on the purchase request lines).\n"
"2. On the RFQ, open the *Alternatives* tab and use *Create Alternative*\n"
"   for each additional vendor, keeping *Copy Products* checked.\n"
"3. Each alternative RFQ line is linked to the same purchase request\n"
"   lines as the original one. The purchase request shows all RFQs in\n"
"   *Purchase Orders*.\n"
"4. Compare the RFQs with *Compare Product Lines*, choose the winning\n"
"   lines and confirm the winning RFQ. The purchase request moves to\n"
"   *Purchased* and the losing RFQs can be cancelled as usual.\n"
"\n"
